# Netlify SPA history fallback.
#
# Client-side routes such as /request and /deliverables are not real files. Without this, a direct
# link or a refresh mid-flow asks Netlify for a file that does not exist and returns 404.
#
# The 200 status matters: a 301 or 302 would change the URL in the address bar and the router would
# lose the route the user actually asked for. Netlify checks real files first, so hashed assets in
# /assets/ are still served normally and never hit this rule.
/*  /index.html  200
